    "hypothesis": "Sorted, contiguous obstacle coordinates avoid the baseline's O(N²) blocked-cell storage. For sparse inputs, combinatorial counting reduces work to O(M²); for denser inputs, a contiguous one-row DP fallback retains O(N²) time without the grid allocation. This tests a locality- and data-layout-oriented approach while keeping work bounded by the better of the two methods asymptotically.",
